Here are a couple of guesses:

I noticed that if you have learned teleport via a spellbook (even if you
already have the intrinsic) the game uses up your spells and spell points.

This makes it interesting for Neutrals and Lawfuls returning from hell.
Hell actually uses up *your* teleport spell and points to 'port you deeper
into Hell on the staircase.

Hell *won't* check to see if you have the intrinsic after it determines
that you don't have enough spell points to cast teleport.  You'll get
the message "You don't have enough points to cast that spell."  if Hell
wants to teleport you down, and it can't use up your memorized spell.

(This enables a cheat:  Simply cast so many spells that you can't cast
teleport every time you want to ascend in Hell, and it's guaranteed never
to 'port you deeper into Hell when you're on the staircase.)

So perhaps when you walked into the pool:

1) You had also "memorized" teleport in addition having the intrinsic, and:
   a) The runes were too hard to make out. (No spells left.)
      I don't think the game checks to see if you have the intrinsic
      after it determines you can't cast the memorized spell.
   b) You didn't have enough spell points to cast the memorized spell.
      (Again, having read the spell overides having the intrinsic.)
2) Or perhaps you were too hungry to 'port out.  (It takes food to cast
   a spell, and you can't do it if you're hungry.  This may even apply to
   intrinsics.)

